{
  "id": "task_005",
  "title": "Edit Distance on RLE-Encoded Strings",
  "language": "python",
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "source": "Custom \u2014 edit distance + run-length encoding",
  "description": "Write a Python function `rle_edit_distance(s: list, t: list) -> int`.\n\nBoth `s` and `t` are run-length encoded (RLE) strings. Each is a list of `[char, count]` pairs, e.g. `[['a', 3], ['b', 2]]` represents `'aaabb'`.\n\nReturn the minimum edit distance (Levenshtein distance) between the two decoded strings. Operations: insert one character (+1 cost), delete one character (+1 cost), replace one character (+1 cost).\n\nAn empty RLE list represents the empty string.\n\nFunction signature:\ndef rle_edit_distance(s: list, t: list) -> int:",
  "function_signature": "def rle_edit_distance(s: list, t: list) -> int:",
  "constraints": [
    "0 <= len(s), len(t) <= 50 (number of RLE groups)",
    "1 <= count <= 100 per group",
    "char is a single lowercase letter",
    "Total decoded length <= 1000"
  ],
